+# Release check blocked: libfoo artifact checksum mismatch
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`test_release_artifacts_verify` (and therefore `python3 verify.py`) cannot pass.
+The `libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` artifact in `artifacts/` does not match its entry in
+`SHA256SUMS`:
+
+| | SHA-256 |
+|---|---|
+| `SHA256SUMS` (expected) | `7bee020ac21efb3831d920af0b8c5efe8d44cdf227ab94847f509188420356bd` |
+| `artifacts/libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` (actual) | `fde9b2575edbefb297fa7d93738b4bb1f09b7f777d1723b90194ad53cd9bc9ce` |
+
+The other two artifacts match their manifest entries (`cli-2.0.1.zip` and
+`docs-2026.10.tar.gz`).
+
+## Why it cannot be fixed here
+
+This is a real content mismatch, not a verifier bug. The expected bytes for the
+artifact are not available anywhere in the repository (there is only the single
+initial commit, which already contains the mismatched artifact), so the
+artifact cannot be restored to a state that produces the manifest's checksum.
+
+The only apparent ways to make the check green here would be to edit
+`SHA256SUMS` to the artifact's current hash, or to skip the test/check. Both
+would bless an unverified (possibly corrupted or tampered-with) release
+artifact and defeat the purpose of the checksum step. Per instructions, no such
+workaround was applied.
+
+## What was fixed
+
+`verify.py` had two genuine bugs that also caused CI failures:
+
+- It read artifacts in text mode and then `.encode()`d the result. That
+  corrupted binary content and raised `UnicodeDecodeError`; artifacts are now
+  read as binary.
+- It compared digests case-sensitively, although manifests (including
+  `SHA256SUMS` and the test fixture) use uppercase hex; the expected digest is
+  now lowercased before comparison.
+
+With those fixes, `test_binary_files` and `test_reports_missing` pass, and the
+verifier now correctly reports exactly `libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` as mismatched.
+
+## What is needed to unblock
+
+Regenerate or re-fetch `libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` from the release build so its
+SHA-256 is `7bee020a...356bd`, or, if `fde9b257...bc9bc9e` is confirmed to be
+the intended artifact, update `SHA256SUMS` through the normal release process
+(rebuild + re-sign the manifest) rather than editing it in this checkout.
